and NOTICE.md. Changes must be identified, and modified versions must not be
represented as official releases.

3. Commercial permission. Prior written permission from the relevant rights
holders is required for selling this project or modified versions, paid licensing,
paid hosting, paid control panels, paid deployment services, or incorporating it
into other commercial products. Contact the maintainers through the official
repository: https://github.com/Z1og/L4D2-Control.

4. Attribution. Distributed code and publicly provided interfaces must retain
clear project attribution and license notices. Copyright and project identity
markers must not be removed or falsified to misrepresent authorship, conceal
origin, or evade commercial authorization. Legitimate modifications may rebuild
the fingerprint while retaining the original project identity and identifying
the modified source.

5. Reserved rights and warranty. Rights not expressly granted are reserved.
The project is provided AS IS, without warranties. To the extent permitted by
applicable law, the rights holders are not liable for losses arising from use.
This license does not revoke rights validly granted for earlier versions and
does not grant rights to third-party trademarks or resources.
